{"caseId":"OD2-HO-STOP-1","answers":[{"itemId":"Q1","answer":"supported","confidence":93,"evidenceIds":["E2","E3","E4","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q2","answer":"contradicted","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q3","answer":"contradicted","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q4","answer":"contradicted","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q5","answer":"unknown","confidence":60,"evidenceIds":["E2","E6"]},{"itemId":"Q6","answer":"causal","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["E3","E4","E5","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q7","answer":"contradicted","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q8","answer":"unknown","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E2","E6"]},{"itemId":"Q9","answer":"contradicted","confidence":87,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q10","answer":"preferred","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["E3"]},{"itemId":"Q11","answer":"harmful","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E2","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q12","answer":"premature","confidence":65,"evidenceIds":["E6","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q13","answer":"acceptable","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E5","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q14","answer":"harmful","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q15","answer":"sufficient","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E3","E4","E5"]}],"brief":"The August drop is almost entirely a cooling failure on floors 6-8. Chiller CH-2 failed on 4 August and wasn't fixed until 19 August. Rooms ran at 26-29°C, against a set point of 22. Floors 6-8 scores fell from 8.6 to 7.4, and room comfort fell from 8.4 to 6.1. Scores for stays ending 5-20 August were 6.8, then recovered to 8.4 once cooling returned. Floors 1-5 were essentially flat at 8.5. Of 74 negative comments, 56 were about heat, all from floors 6-8. Front-desk temperature complaints went from 1 to 24.

Cleanliness scores are flat at 8.6-8.7, and in-house inspection pass rates are unchanged at 95-96%. Kiosk use, queue times and check-in scores are also steady. So don't give notice to Orrin and don't pull the kiosks. The evidence doesn't support either move. Don't exclude the August floors 6-8 responses from the reported score either. That would hide a real failure.

Next steps: restore the deferred preventive maintenance on both chillers, keep critical spares on site, and write a guest-recovery protocol for cooling outages. The 6% rate rise is unproven as a cause. Its effect can't be separated from the usual August dip in value scores, so keep watching value scores. I'm fairly confident in this, and I didn't collect any extra evidence."}
